# orchestrator-workflow local run state (orchestration bookkeeping,
# never committed). Root-anchored so it only matches the top-level .ai/,
# not an unrelated .ai fixture nested inside a package or test tree.
# .ai/workflow/ (kit templates + manifest.json) is intentionally NOT
# ignored: those files are committed so the kit survives fresh clones.
/.ai/runs/

# Locally-installed agent tooling (orchestrator-workflow kit adapter layer,
# deliberately NOT versioned here - decision recorded in task c0c672f0,
# matching the harness precedent). The versioned kit surface is
# .ai/workflow/** only; the adapter layer (AGENTS.md marker section,
# CLAUDE.md, .claude/, plus .agents/ and .opencode/ for the codex and
# opencode harnesses) is materialized per machine by
# `npx orchestrator-workflow init`, and the operating procedure lives in
# the orchestrator-workflow package (github.com/LanNguyenSi/agent-dx).
# See .ai/workflow/README.md. Root-anchored per this file's convention:
# the installer only writes at repo root, and unanchored patterns would
# also swallow nested fixtures in a repo whose product domain is agent
# instructions. These lines keep a plain `init` from leaving
# accidentally-commitable files behind.
/.claude/
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/.agents/
/.opencode/
